{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nReplaying a candidate change tells you *what would change*, not whether it is *better*. The store already carries outcome signals needing no LLM/human labeling: revise→re-review pairs (2,483; per-finding survival via `norm_id`), verdict flips on byte-identical material (208; the reviewer-noise floor), bug closes with `close_class=plan_defect` (84), `caused_by` links (89), PASS-then-completion-FAIL tickets (199), reopens (18).\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py` (celestine-treasonous-ewe, closed) exists: `build_corpus(store_roots, *, cache_dir) -> manifest` recovers PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE `plan_review_result_v1/v2` sidecars, reconstructs at-review material from CREATE/EDIT/FILE_IMPACT events ONLY, verifies against `material_fingerprint`, and returns `manifest[\"content_hash\"]` (the corpus identity) — `_compute_manifest`'s actual keys are `stores`, `schema_histogram`, `verdict_histogram`, `verified_count`, `unverified_count`, `verified_ratio`, `verified_by_generation`, `row_count`, `content_hash`; no build timestamp. `store_roots` is `{store_name: tracker_git_root}` (the `.tickets-tracker` DIR itself).\n\n`config.tracker_dir_override()` (`_config_sources.py:117-131`) reads `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` and, when set, that value WINS VERBATIM over every other resolution path (config file, `repo_root`-relative default) — `tracker_dir()` returns it directly, before even trying `load_config`. `show_ticket(ticket_id, *, repo_root=None, include_inbound=False)` goes through `tracker_dir()`, so pointing `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` at a `store_roots` tracker dir makes `show_ticket` read exactly that store regardless of any project-level `tracker.dir` config or renamed layout — a `repo_root`-parent guess would silently break under either. A `caused_by` link is stored as a single OUTBOUND edge on the SOURCE (a bug), pointing at its TARGET (the culprit/origin ticket) — so `caused_by` appears in the bug's own `deps` (outbound) and, symmetrically, in the CULPRIT's `inbound_deps` (via `include_inbound=True`) — never the reverse.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py`:\n\n- **Corpus identity**: call `corpus.build_corpus(store_roots, cache_dir=...)`; `manifest[\"content_hash\"]` is the hash labels key to. `labels.py` refuses (raises, naming both hashes) if a caller-supplied `labels-<hash>.jsonl`'s hash disagrees with a freshly recomputed `build_corpus(...)[\"content_hash\"]`.\n- **Finding-level source**: reuse `corpus._enumerate_event_blobs` + `corpus._batch_cat` to re-read recovered `REVIEW_RESULT` blobs' raw `data` (`kind == \"REVIEW_RESULT\"`, `data.schema in corpus._SCHEMAS`) — the full body. Filter each sidecar's `findings` to `sidecar.surfaced_findings(data)` (`SURFACED_DECISIONS = (\"block\", \"advisory\")`) before any `norm_id` join — the unfiltered array also carries overflow/indeterminate/dropped entries (bug old-frilly-plankton).\n- **Ticket-level event source (multi-store, via env override, not path-guessing)**: for each `store_name, tracker_git_root` in `store_roots`, temporarily set `os.environ[\"REBAR_TRACKER_DIR\"] = tracker_git_root` (restoring the prior value, or unsetting, in a `finally`) around every `show_ticket(ticket_id, include_inbound=True)` call for that store's corpus tickets — this makes `show_ticket` read exactly `tracker_git_root` regardless of that store's own `tracker.dir` config, verbatim, per `tracker_dir_override()`'s precedence. `reopen_count`/`force_close`/`completion_verifier_fail_count` reuse `mine_outcome_corpus.py`'s pure functions of that name, fed from `labels.py`'s own per-store git-walk (extending `corpus._enumerate_event_blobs`'s content-type filter to also recover STATUS/COMMENT/COMPLETION_VERDICT blobs) — covering every store, not just the miner's local-tracker-only frozen artifact.\n- **Ticket-level labels**: `escaped_defect(X)` = UNION of two disjuncts evaluated on the SAME ticket id X: (a) `X.close_class == \"plan_defect\"` from X's own compiled state (only ever true when X is itself a bug ticket); (b) X carries an inbound `caused_by` edge — `X.inbound_deps` contains an entry with `relation == \"caused_by\"` (present only when some OTHER ticket, a bug, has an outbound `caused_by` edge naming X as its culprit). `completion_failed_after_pass` (`completion_verifier_fail_count > 0` after a PASS); `reopened` (`reopen_count > 0`); `clean_close` (closed, no escape signals, closed ≥`CLEAN_CLOSE_MIN_DAYS` days — named constant, default 7 — before the labels RUN time, `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` at the point `labels.py` executes, NOT a corpus-carried timestamp — an accepted, explicitly-documented imprecision unlike the hash-pinned deterministic labels above). Each label carries its source event id(s).\n- **Finding-level labels**: for consecutive reviews (surfaced findings only) with changed material, join by `norm_id`; `resolved_by_author` (present in k, absent in k+1, material changed) vs `persisted`; `noise_flip` for identical-material pairs.\n- **Noise floor**: over identical-material pairs (same `material_fingerprint` across consecutive reviews): (a) verdict flip rate; (b) per-criterion finding churn (Jaccard by `norm_id`); (c) per-question Pass-2 agreement — the persisted `verification` field is a NESTED dict, `{\"binary\": {key: value, ...}, \"severity_attributes\": {key: value, ...}}`; flatten each sub-dict's keys as `\"binary.<key>\"` / `\"severity_attributes.<key>\"` before comparing. For each `norm_id` present in BOTH reviews of a pair with a `verification` dict in both, compare each flattened key present in BOTH findings' flattened maps; agreement is micro-averaged: `(# flattened-key-comparisons where old value == new value) / (total flattened-key-comparisons)`, pooled across every finding and every pair (one figure, plus the pooled comparison count published alongside it).\n- Output `labels-<content_hash>.jsonl` plus a Markdown report with per-label-source counts, joined to `content_hash`.\n\nLabel definitions are constants in one module so a later ticket can tighten them.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/labels-report-<date>.md` (new)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_labels.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: synthetic corpus of five tickets exercising each ticket label and each finding label — including a bug ticket satisfying `escaped_defect` via `close_class` and a SEPARATE origin ticket satisfying it via `inbound_deps`; identical-material pair with a verdict flip counted as noise, changed-material pair not; a permanently-dropped finding excluded from the `norm_id` join; per-question agreement computed correctly over a nested `verification` dict with one matching and one mismatching flattened key (expect 0.5); `clean_close`'s day-arithmetic against a monkeypatched \"now\". A ticket resolved via the `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` override round-trips correctly and the env var is restored afterward (proven by reading a DIFFERENT ticket from the original/default tracker in the same test process, after the override call returns). Empty corpus → empty report. A `labels-<hash>.jsonl` built against a stale `content_hash` is refused when re-verified.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every review and finding in the corpus carries the labels above, with source event ids; checked by the labels report counts matching independent `jq` counts over the store for `plan_defect`, `caused_by` and reopen events.\n- [ ] The noise floor (verdict flip rate, per-criterion churn, per-question agreement with its pooled comparison count) is published with the identical-material pair count it was computed from; checked in the report.\n- [ ] Labels are keyed to `corpus.build_corpus(...)[\"content_hash\"]` and the loader raises when a fresh recompute disagrees with a supplied file's hash; checked by a unit test.\n- [ ] No LLM calls; checked by running with no provider credentials."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788065653897964349,"uuid":"ef30378c-1b22-40aa-8318-547229973a72"}